Subject: [PATCH 34/39] =?UTF-8?q?hottyterm:=20key=20names=20are=20myelin?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20key=20names=200.1=20(HOTTY=200.4,=20SPEC=20=C2=A710.4)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A press is offered to hotty-blitz by two names, as 0.4's C ABI takes them:
its physical key (ctrl+key_w) and the character it types (ctrl+w), the
modifiers in the order super, ctrl, alt, shift. A modifier tapped alone is
named on its release, sided and as a modifier key (shift_left, shift).
An edit command's key is the one name its bytes would carry (SPEC §10.6).
Menus' cells_key and the copy keys take both names too.
